ves making or making it  easy for me to imply that he's using  some additional sensors in order to  recognize the gestures that he's making  and so  all right so obviously gesture  recognition it's not it's not a novel  problem many companies tried or actually  have built just a recognition system but  they didn't really gain a wider  acceptance among Google users and this  is also why it is also because they  often or always required some additional  sensors so for example you might see the  wireless glove that has different  sensors attached to the glove which  gives extra information based on this  information women we make a  classification or Microsoft Kinect has a  depth camera there were some systems  that were segmenting the body and based  on the segmentation they predicted the  gesture and so on the contrary we  decided to try just feeding a neural  network with huge amount of data and  seeing if we can do it without any  additional devices and so this is  important because it means that the end  user in the end would only need a webcam  or a laptop camera to be able to use a  gesture recognition system yeah and  obviously for the deep learning for any  kind of deep learning algorithms we need  huge amounts of data data in magnitudes  of thousands or even hundreds of  thousands and the natural question is  how do we get this kind of data for this  very specific problem that we've chose  so for example you could try data  crawling so scraping the videos from the  internet but this is obviously not ideal  because first of all this is a very  time-consuming problem you might not  find the right amount of data you might  find that the classes that you chose are  not balanced because there are thousands  of videos of thumbs up by only few of  some kind of gesture that you want your  system to be able to recognize you might  find that the video  contain multiple people performing  multiple gesture or the same gestures  Metheny ously or at different time steps  y